Refresh the tray context menu in place instead of recreating the Tray.

The frontend syncs the quick-entry shortcut to the main process every
time settings load (auth store), and the handler responded by destroying
and recreating the Tray. On Linux the StatusNotifierItem spec has no
unregister call - hosts only drop items when the owning D-Bus connection
dies - so every rebuild leaked a ghost tray icon (11+ icons after a day).

